# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 6 of the Tutorial (Part 2)

[Bo2's Example 5.6 (DC, before the switch)]

e,2,0,10
r1,2,1,1
c,1,0,1/4
r4,1,0,4

analysis: dc
note: A three-interval problem: one switch opens at t = 0 and another closes at t = 1 s. Find vc(t) and ic(t) for all t; this first interval in DC gives vc = 8 V.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-5-6-14.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 5.6 (TR, 0 < t <= 1 s)]

c,1,0,1/4,8
r4,1,0,4

analysis: tr
note: Second interval: vc and ic decay as e^(-t) from the 8 V initial condition.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-5-6-14.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 5.6 (TR, t > 1 s)]

c,1,0,1/4,2.943
re,1,0,[4,6]

analysis: tr
note: Third interval, after the second switch closes. t here counts from the start of this interval, so the chapter writes the answer with (t-1) in it. The initial condition is the previous interval's voltage at t = 1.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-5-6-14.jpg
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.6 (DC)]

e,1,0,9
r9,1,0,9
r3,1,2,3
l,2,0,6

analysis: dc
note: Another problem whose switch moves at a time other than zero — t = 2 s. Find iL(t) and vL(t) for all t; this first interval in DC gives il = 3 A.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-6-17.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.6 (TR, 0 < t <= 2 s)]

r,1,0,9+3
l,1,0,6,3

analysis: tr
note: Second interval: il and vl decay as e^(-2t).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-6-17.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.6 (TR, t > 2 s)]

r,1,0,[9+3,4]
l,1,0,6,.055

analysis: tr
note: Third interval, starting from the 0.055 A the second interval left at t = 2 s; the chapter writes the answers with (t-2) in them.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-6-17.jpg
rounding: 3
si: no
units: yes


